    "turn_text": "the next wave podcast. Hashtag no filter. All right, next way, welcome back. Family is so good to be talking to y'all today. I want to officially welcome you to the final installment of our hashtag No Filter podcast series. So today's episode will be entitled, Next Waiver's Breaking Barriers. We wanna hit on a few things. We wanna talk about volunteer member organizing again, VMO. So you know we've definitely talked about that before. I wanna share some of the stories that I've seen as I've traveled around the country and visited some next wave chapters. And then also, I got a very special treat for you guys. AFSCME's very own Secretary of Treasurer, Alyssa McBride, has a speaker series called Ideas at AFSCME. And on this speaker series, she brings in dynamic individuals from all across the United States to come in and sit with some AFSCME members and just talk about some of the work that they're doing and how that work impacts us as AFSCME members. And so not too long ago, one of her guests was a young congresswoman, Abby Finkenauer, out of Iowa's first district. She came down to talk and I got to ask her a couple questions as well. And I must say that while speaking with her, I definitely felt a familiar vibe. It felt like I was talking to a friend or someone that I had grown up with. And so that was very encouraging for me.",
